Nothing checks a commit message before it reaches the list, so a
missing prefix or an overlong line costs a review round to catch.
Make format-patch.sh refuse a series, writing nothing, when a subject
lacks an "area: " prefix or runs over 72 characters, or a body line
runs over 72 or has a double space between words. Warn, without
refusing, on a diff over 200 lines. The rules that need judgement stay
prose in doc/style/commit.md.
